🔄 DATA FLOW EXAMPLE
User creates a form field:
plain
Copy
1. Browser: User drags "Email" from ComponentPalette
         ↓
2. DND: @dnd-kit detects drop on Canvas
         ↓
3. Store: formBuilderStore.addComponent('email')
         - Creates new component object
         - Adds to schema.components array
         - Saves to history (for undo)
         - Updates updatedAt timestamp
         ↓
4. UI: Canvas re-renders with new component
         ↓
5. Auto-save: useAutoSave hook detects change
         ↓
6. API: POST /api/forms/{id} with new schema
         ↓
7. Backend: FormService.update() validates, saves to PostgreSQL
         ↓
8. WebSocket: Broadcasts change to other editors in same room
         ↓
9. Other Users: Their UI updates with live cursor + new field
